# agent-engine — local environment template.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      # then set ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID
#                             # and run: gcloud auth application-default login
#
# Nothing in this repo loads .env implicitly (no dotenv dependency anywhere).
# It's read only by the root scripts that pass Node's own --env-file flag:
# `npm run dev:server`, `npm run start:server`, and
# `npm run smoke:agent-platform`. Every other command (build, typecheck, test,
# demo:*, smoke) needs no environment at all.
#
# Every variable below is read by exactly one factory — the file named in the
# comment above it is the authority, not this template.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required to boot apps/agent-server
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# packages/core/src/router/create-model-router-from-env.ts
#
# Which network path the "pinned" tier — the tier every agent in this system
# declares — takes to Claude. Both routes reach the SAME models, so this never
# changes a model, a prompt, an alias, or a price; only the transport and the
# credential. Model ids stay in canonical Claude API form everywhere except
# inside the Agent Platform adapter, which translates them at the boundary
# (router/adapters/agent-platform-model-ids.ts).
#
#   agent-platform  (default)  Google Cloud's Agent Platform, formerly Vertex
#                              AI. Authenticates with Application Default
#                              Credentials — no key in any env var, which is
#                              the point (RFC-01 §16.3).
#   anthropic                  Direct to the Anthropic API with a key. The
#                              local-dev path if you have no GCP access, and
#                              the escape hatch during an Agent Platform
#                              incident.
#   vertex                     Accepted as an alias for agent-platform.
#
# MODEL_PROVIDER=agent-platform

# Required on the agent-platform route: the GCP project whose Model Garden has
# the Claude models enabled. GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT (further down) is used as a
# fallback, so a Cloud Run deployment that already sets it needs nothing extra.
# The router throws at startup naming this variable if neither is set.
#
# Auth is ADC ONLY — there is deliberately no key-file or access-token branch:
#   locally:    gcloud auth application-default login
#   Cloud Run:  the attached service account (roles/aiplatform.user)
ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID=your-gcp-project-id

# Endpoint for the agent-platform route. "global" (the default when unset) has
# the best availability and the fewest 429s. Also accepts a multi-region
# ("us", "eu") or a specific region ("us-east5", "europe-west1").
# VERTEX_AI_LOCATION is read as a fallback, since this repo already carries it
# for the Vertex-backed prompt store. A value that isn't shaped like a region
# is treated as unset rather than sent to the API.
# CLOUD_ML_REGION=global

# Per-model region pin, for a model the endpoint above doesn't serve — the
# common cause of a 404 "model not found" on CLOUD_ML_REGION=global. Both the
# dated and undated forms of a model id are accepted, most specific first:
# VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_HAIKU_4_5=us-east5
# VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_SONNET_4_6=europe-west1

# Override the Agent Platform endpoint URL — for a private endpoint or a
# gateway in front of it. Almost never needed.
# ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_BASE_URL=

# Required on the anthropic route (MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic). On the DEFAULT
# agent-platform route, setting this ALSO opts into ResilientClaudeAdapter's
# dual-layer fallback (create-model-router-from-env.ts): a 429 (quota
# exhausted) or 404 (model/region not served) from Vertex AI Model Garden
# retries the SAME model directly against the real Anthropic API instead —
# same model id, different transport, never a silent model swap. Leave unset
# entirely only if you want zero fallback and a bare Agent Platform adapter.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-replace-me

# The absolute last resort, after BOTH Claude routes above have been tried
# and failed: Vertex AI Gemini, a genuinely different model family. Only
# engages when a Gemini vendor adapter is ALSO configured (GEMINI_VERTEX_
# PROJECT_ID or GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT, or GEMINI_API_KEY on GEMINI_ROUTE=direct
# — see the Gemini vendor section below). Defaults to "gemini-1.5-flash".
#
# In a deployment where GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT is set to a DIFFERENT project
# than ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID (e.g. Firestore lives in one project,
# Vertex AI Model Garden access in another — see this repo's own prep/prod
# split), set GEMINI_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID explicitly to match
# ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID. Otherwise createGeminiVendorAdapter's own
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT fallback silently points Gemini at the wrong project.
# CLAUDE_FALLBACK_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-1.5-flash

# Set to any value to send no prompt-cache breakpoints at all. The adapter
# otherwise caches the stable tools+system prefix of every step, which is
# where the 90% cache-read discount comes from — only turn this off to isolate
# a caching-related behaviour change while debugging.
# DISABLE_PROMPT_CACHING=1

# Whichever route is selected: real model calls cost money on every
# POST /api/v1/runs/start.

# packages/core/src/agent/create-prompt-store-from-env.ts
# "memory" (the default) starts EMPTY — every skillRef resolution then fails,
# so it is not a usable local setting. Use "file" plus the root below.
# "firestore"/"vertex" need GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT; "vertex" additionally has no
# client wired up in this build (see apps/agent-server/src/wiring/prompt-store.ts).
PROMPT_STORE_DRIVER=file

# Required whenever PROMPT_STORE_DRIVER=file. FilePromptStore expects ONE root
# laid out as <root>/<promptId>/<version>.md, but the prompts ship per agent
# (agents/x-agent/prompts/x-craft/1.md, ...). `npm run setup:local` assembles
# every agent's prompts into the single directory below.
PROMPT_STORE_FILE_ROOT=./.local/prompts

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local storage — omit all of these and you get in-process/on-disk defaults
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# packages/tools/common/src/adapters/file-git/workspace-store.ts
# Client profiles, topic catalog, memory, ledger. Defaults to ./.karos-workspace.
# A run against an EMPTY workspace stops at 00-intake-check with
# status "blocked_intake" — `npm run setup:local` seeds a demo tenant.
KAROS_WORKSPACE_ROOT=./.local/workspace

# apps/agent-server/src/server.ts — Cloud Run injects this; 8080 if unset.
PORT=8080

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GCP — storage and telemetry
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave these unset locally EXCEPT as noted: GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT is also the
# fallback project for the agent-platform model route above, so setting it
# locally to satisfy the router additionally switches the stores below onto
# real GCP services. Set ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID instead if you want the
# model route on GCP while everything else stays local — that is the usual
# local setup.
#
# Setting GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT switches the durable store from
# MemoryDurableStepStore to a real Firestore client (apps/agent-server/src/
# wiring/durable-store.ts) and requires Application Default Credentials
# (`gcloud auth application-default login`). Setting GCS_WORKSPACE_BUCKET does
# the same for client state (wiring/workspace-store.ts). Both are for a real
# Cloud Run deployment, where in-process state would not survive a resume
# landing on a different instance.
#
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=
# FIRESTORE_DATABASE_ID=(default)
# GCS_WORKSPACE_BUCKET=
# VERTEX_AI_LOCATION=us-central1
# PROMPT_STORE_TTL_MS=

# apps/agent-server/src/wiring/gcs-artifact-stores.ts (Task 1/Task 2, GCS media &
# artifact storage). Both undefined by default, which keeps every consumer's
# pre-GCS behavior unchanged:
#
#   GCS_MEDIA_BUCKET      publish.renderCarousel's upload target (rendered
#                         Instagram carousel PNGs) — unset, it writes local
#                         scratch PNGs exactly as before. video.uploadDeliverable
#                         (branded-shorts MP4s) and landing.uploadSiteBundle
#                         (Landing Builder site files) take their own
#                         mediaStore/artifactStore param directly, since
#                         neither karos-video nor karos-landing is wired into
#                         this server yet (see packages/tools/src/index.ts's
#                         own doc comment on why `video.*`/`landing.*` are
#                         excluded from createAllKarosTools).
#   GCS_ARTIFACTS_BUCKET  FirestoreDurableStepStore's Task-2 dual-storage
#                         archive target — a step/slot output whose JSON
#                         would exceed Firestore's ~1 MiB document limit
#                         uploads here instead, leaving a {archived, gcsUri,
#                         sizeBytes} placeholder in Firestore. Unset, an
#                         oversized write still goes straight to Firestore
#                         (and still throws there past the real limit).
#
# In karoscmo-prep specifically, the real provisioned buckets are named
# "karoscmo-prep-media-assets" / "karoscmo-prep-agent-artifacts" — NOT
# "karoscmo-media-prep"/"karoscmo-artifacts-prep". Use the real names.
#
# GCS_MEDIA_BUCKET=karoscmo-prep-media-assets
# GCS_ARTIFACTS_BUCKET=karoscmo-prep-agent-artifacts

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional — additional model VENDORS (create-model-router-from-env.ts).
#
# `anthropic` (above) is the only vendor every agent in this system uses by
# default and the only one this router requires configuration for. A step
# switches vendor either in its own source (`ModelPolicy.vendor`) or, without
# touching code, via the per-step override pair below. Each vendor is built
# only if its own section here is configured; a step that requests an
# unconfigured vendor fails loudly and specifically at the point of use
# (DefaultModelRouter's own error), not at startup — so leaving all of this
# unset changes nothing for a deployment that never touches non-Anthropic
# models.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- gemini vendor ---
#
# Which network path Gemini calls take. Same shape as MODEL_PROVIDER above,
# scoped to Gemini — a deployment can run Claude on Agent Platform and Gemini
# direct (or vice versa) independently.
#
#   agent-platform  (default)  Google Cloud's Agent Platform (Vertex AI
#                              backend). ADC only, same as Claude's route.
#   direct                     The Gemini Developer API with GEMINI_API_KEY.
#   vertex                     Accepted as an alias for agent-platform.
#
# GEMINI_ROUTE=agent-platform

# Required on the agent-platform route: the GCP project whose Vertex AI has
# Gemini enabled. GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT is used as a fallback, matching
# ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID's own fallback above.
# GEMINI_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID=your-gcp-project-id

# Endpoint region for the agent-platform route. Falls back to
# CLOUD_ML_REGION / VERTEX_AI_LOCATION, then "global", matching the Claude
# route's own defaulting.
# GEMINI_VERTEX_LOCATION=global

# Per-model region pin, for a Gemini model the endpoint above doesn't serve:
# GEMINI_REGION_GEMINI_2_5_PRO=us-east5

# Required on the direct route (GEMINI_ROUTE=direct) instead of a GCP project.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- model-garden vendor ---
#
# Agent Platform's own Model-as-a-Service OpenAI-compatible endpoint —
# third-party/open Model Garden models (Llama, Mistral, and similar). ADC
# only, same auth story as the Claude and Gemini Agent Platform routes; no
# separate credential beyond a project id. Deliberately gated on its own
# variable rather than falling back to GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT (see the doc
# comment on `createModelGardenVendorAdapter`) — a vendor switch this
# consequential should be a deliberate opt-in, not an accident of which other
# GCP features happen to already be configured. Set it to the same value as
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT to opt in with zero new project setup.
# MODEL_GARDEN_PROJECT_ID=your-gcp-project-id

# Most Model Garden partner models are far more region-restricted than
# Claude/Gemini's own global endpoints. Defaults to "us-central1".
# MODEL_GARDEN_REGION=us-central1

# Per-model region pin:
# MODEL_GARDEN_REGION_LLAMA_3_3_70B_INSTRUCT_MAAS=us-central1

# --- openai-compatible vendor ---
#
# The real OpenAI API, or a self-hosted gateway (LiteLLM) fronting whatever it
# fronts. Distinct from model-garden above even though both share the same
# adapter's wire mechanics — this one is NOT Agent Platform and carries its
# own credential.
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_BASE_URL=
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_API_KEY=

# --- per-step override, any vendor ---
#
# packages/core/src/router/step-model-policy.ts
#
# Overrides ONE step's vendor+model without touching its source, e.g. to try
# a specific agent on Gemini or a Model Garden model before switching its code
# default. <STEP_ID> is the step's own `id` (from its AgentStepConfig),
# upper-cased with every non-alphanumeric run collapsed to one underscore —
# "blog-draft" -> "BLOG_DRAFT", "instagram-image-vet" -> "INSTAGRAM_IMAGE_VET".
# Setting the vendor without also setting the model throws at startup: a
# step's default model id is shaped for its default vendor and will not
# resolve against a different one.
#
# MODEL_STEP_BLOG_DRAFT_VENDOR=gemini
# MODEL_STEP_BLOG_DRAFT_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional — running jobs from a queue (packages/queue, apps/agent-server).
#
# QUEUE_PROVIDER selects the vendor behind the generic QueueAdapter interface
# — the queue-vendor counterpart to MODEL_PROVIDER above. "pubsub" is the only
# implemented value today; a future provider adds a new value here, never
# touches a publisher or consumer. See README's "Running jobs from a queue
# (Pub/Sub)" section for the full setup and both consumption models (push and
# pull).
#
# QUEUE_PROVIDER=pubsub

# --- pubsub provider ---
#
# packages/queue/src/create-queue-from-env.ts
#
# Required: the GCP project whose Pub/Sub this deployment uses.
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT is used as a fallback, matching every other GCP client
# factory in this repo. Auth is Application Default Credentials only — same
# rule as everywhere else (RFC-01 §16.3).
# PUBSUB_PROJECT_ID=your-gcp-project-id

# Topic run-job messages are published to (scripts/queue-publish-demo.ts, or
# any real caller — as of this writing that's karosCMO's own
# AGENT_ENGINE_PUBSUB_TOPIC, src/lib/agent-engine/pubsub-client.ts: the two
# MUST name the same topic, there is no shared config source that enforces
# this for you). Defaults to "agent-engine-run-jobs".
# QUEUE_TOPIC_RUN_JOBS=agent-engine-run-jobs

# Subscription the PULL-based consumer (apps/agent-server/src/queue-consumer.ts
# — local dev, or a dedicated always-on worker) reads from. Defaults to
# "agent-engine-run-jobs-pull". Not used by the PUSH route below at all —
# Pub/Sub delivers directly to it over HTTP instead of this server pulling.
# QUEUE_SUBSCRIPTION_RUN_JOBS=agent-engine-run-jobs-pull

# --- push route (apps/agent-server/src/routes/queue.ts): POST /api/v1/queue/pubsub-push ---
#
# Unset (the default) is a permissive local-dev config: the push route
# accepts any syntactically valid envelope, no auth checked at all — fine
# until something has actually been configured to push here.
#
# Required for real OIDC identity-token verification in production: the
# EXACT HTTPS URL Pub/Sub is configured to push to (its own subscription's
# push-endpoint, with --push-auth-service-account set) — this is the
# expected `audience` on the token. Unknown until after the first deploy (the
# Cloud Run URL is assigned at deploy time); set it via `gcloud run services
# update --update-env-vars` once you know it. Never leave this unset once a
# real push subscription is pointed at this service.
# PUBSUB_PUSH_AUDIENCE_URL=https://your-service-xxxxx-uc.a.run.app/api/v1/queue/pubsub-push

# ── media.findImages image sourcing (packages/tools/karos-media) ──────────────
# All optional. The keyless providers (openverse, wikimedia, ddg_images) give
# every deployment a working image chain with none of these set; each key only
# ADDS a source. See packages/tools/karos-media/README.md for the route order.
#
# Unsplash: the "Access Key" from unsplash.com/oauth/applications, NOT the
# secret key (that is for OAuth user flows, which this engine does not use).
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=
# Pexels: a free key from pexels.com/api. Sent as a bare `Authorization`
# header value, with no "Bearer " prefix.
PEXELS_API_KEY=
# Pixabay: a free key from pixabay.com/api/docs. Passed as a `key` query param.
PIXABAY_API_KEY=
# Google Places: enable the Places API, then create an API key.
GOOGLE_PLACES_KEY=

# ── ScrappyCoco: the generic scraper (packages/tools/karos-scraper) ───────────
# Backs research.pull's live sources AND the visual pipeline's scrape tier.
# Without it research.pull reports not_available and content agents hold rather
# than drafting from a placeholder, so treat it as required to produce content.
# Auth header is X-API-Key. Optional override: SCRAPPYCOCO_BASE_URL.
SCRAPPYCOCO_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Service-to-service authentication (AU1 / SCRUM-287)
# apps/agent-server/src/auth/service-identity.ts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Deliberately the same four names agent-middleware's app/security.py uses, so
# one operator reads one vocabulary across both services.
#
# Unset (the default) means DISABLED: every request is let through, which is
# correct for local development and is the behaviour the test suite relies on.
# Deployed environments set AUTH_ENABLED=true.
#
# AUTH_ENABLED=true
#
# This service's own URL, and the ONLY value a caller's token `aud` may carry.
# Required whenever AUTH_ENABLED is true: without it the service fails every
# request closed (500) rather than verifying signatures without an audience,
# which would accept any Google-signed token in existence.
#
# It must match karosCMO's own AGENT_ENGINE_AUDIENCE exactly — that is the
# audience the portal already mints its identity tokens for. A mismatch 401s
# every call. Cloud Run only assigns the URL at deploy time, so this has the
# same chicken-and-egg as PUBSUB_PUSH_AUDIENCE_URL above: deploy once, then set it.
#
# AUTH_AUDIENCE=https://agent-engine-prep-xxxxxxxx-uc.a.run.app
#
# Comma-separated service-account emails permitted to call. Empty means "any
# identity Google vouches for for this audience", which is only safe because
# Cloud Run IAM (roles/run.invoker) already restricts who can reach the service
# at all. Populate it for defence in depth — the portal's SA is the only real
# caller today.
#
# AUTH_ALLOWED_SERVICE_ACCOUNTS=portal@karoscmo.iam.gserviceaccount.com
#
# Static bearer token for curl and local portals. Refused outright when the
# deployment reads as production (FIRESTORE_DATABASE_ID != "prep"), so a stray
# value on a production deploy cannot become a total auth bypass.
#
# AUTH_DEV_TOKEN=
#
# NOTE: authentication here identifies the CALLER, not the tenant. The portal's
# single service account legitimately acts for every client, so `clientSlug`
# remains caller-asserted and trusted. True per-tenant entitlement needs the
# portal to forward an end-user-scoped claim (or per-tenant service accounts)
# and is tracked separately.

# =============================================================================
# Variables read by code that this file did not document (AU49 / SCRUM-332)
# =============================================================================
# `npx tsx scripts/config-inventory.ts` finds these by reading the source, and
# CI fails when the list is non-empty. Each entry says what it does, whether it
# is required, and — the part that matters most — WHAT HAPPENS WHEN IT IS
# ABSENT, because several of these downgrade a capability instead of failing.
# The runtime view of the same question is
# GET /api/v1/diagnostics/capabilities (AU55).

# ── Telemetry sink ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Which project/dataset receives per-step cost and token rows.
# BQ_PROJECT_ID falls back to GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT, BQ_DATASET_ID to
# "bi_telemetry". ABSENT: cost rows are still written to the fallback target;
# a WRONG value writes to a table nobody reads, which is the failure that made
# prep's telemetry vanish into production's dataset once already.
# BQ_PROJECT_ID=
# BQ_DATASET_ID=

# ── Video engine (branded-shorts, tiktok) ────────────────────────────────────
# BRANDED_SHORTS_ENGINE_DIR is REQUIRED for any video run: the Python engine
# checkout holding cut_check.py, brand_check.py, graphic_qa.py and the render
# pipeline. ABSENT: every video.* gate returns tooling_error naming it, and a
# branded-shorts run fails rather than shipping unchecked footage.
# BRANDED_SHORTS_ENGINE_DIR=
# Optional scratch root for intermediate render artefacts; defaults to a temp
# directory. ABSENT: renders use the system temp dir.
# BRANDED_SHORTS_WORK_ROOT=
# Optional interpreter/binary overrides for that engine. ABSENT: "python3",
# "ffmpeg" and "ffprobe" are resolved from PATH, which is correct in the
# container and usually wrong on a Mac without them installed.
# KAROS_VIDEO_PYTHON_BIN=
# KAROS_VIDEO_FFMPEG_BIN=
# KAROS_VIDEO_FFPROBE_BIN=

# ── Dynamic code steps ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Off unless "true". Runs Studio-authored code in a sandbox. ABSENT (the
# default): a dynamic agent definition containing a code stage fails that stage
# rather than executing it. Deliberately off — the sandbox has had no security
# review (see packages/dynamic-sandbox/src/code-sandbox.ts).
# DYNAMIC_CODE_STEPS_ENABLED=
# Optional container image for the hardened Docker tier. ABSENT: the sandbox
# falls back to the in-process local tier with interpreter-level guards.
# DYNAMIC_CODE_SANDBOX_IMAGE=

# ── Reputation capture ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional, one per review platform. ABSENT: that leg writes an UNAVAILABLE
# tombstone instead of reviews — the pulse still runs, and the gap stays
# visible rather than reading as "no reviews this month".
# GOOGLE_BUSINESS_TOKEN=
# YELP_API_KEY=

# ── Video/image generation model selection ───────────────────────────────────
# Optional overrides. ABSENT: image.generate uses gemini-2.5-flash-image in
# VERTEX_AI_LOCATION. Imagen model ids 404 in this project — see
# packages/tools/karos-media/src/generate-image.ts before changing these.
# IMAGE_GEN_MODEL=
# IMAGE_GEN_LOCATION=
# VIDEO_GEN_MODEL=

# ── Landing builder roots ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED for landing-builder runs: where the FORGE-proven template kit is
# checked out, and where generated sites/bundles are written. ABSENT: every
# landing.* tool returns tooling_error, so a landing run cannot start.
# LANDING_ENGINE_TEMPLATE_ROOT=
# LANDING_ENGINE_ROOT=
# LANDING_ENGINE_CLIENTS_ROOT=
# LANDING_ENGINE_BUNDLES_ROOT=

# ── instagram-agent render root ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED to dispatch instagram-agent: publish.renderCarousel bounds every
# templateDir/outDir/image path under this root with assertInside(). ABSENT:
# buildWorkflowForProduct throws a specific error rather than rendering
# outside a fence.
# INSTAGRAM_AGENT_REPO_ROOT=

# ── Model router extras ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. OPENAI_API_KEY is accepted as a fallback for
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_API_KEY. ABSENT: the openai-compatible vendor is not built,
# and a step naming it fails loudly at the point of use rather than silently
# rerouting.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Optional region for the Vertex-backed prompt store; falls back to
# VERTEX_AI_LOCATION. ABSENT: the fallback is used.
# GCP_REGION=

# ── Scraper endpoint override ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Points the generic ScraperProvider at a non-default endpoint.
# ABSENT: the vendor's documented base URL is used.
# SCRAPPYCOCO_BASE_URL=

# ── Video transcription ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED for any branded-shorts or tiktok run: speech-to-text over the source
# video, which every cut decision is made from. ABSENT: video.transcribe
# reports not_available and the run cannot plan a cut at all.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
